KEKS -- an ERP system for a school canteen
==========================================

KEKS is an ERP system for a school canteen.  It is a Telegram bot
written in Python with the aiogram library, keeping its data in
PostgreSQL.

A Russian version of this file is in README.ru.

Requirements
------------

Python 3 with the packages in requirements.txt, and a PostgreSQL
server.

Using it
--------

 1. Clone this repository.

 2. Go to the project's directory.

 3. Set up your PostgreSQL server and fill in all the needed
    information in config.ini.

 4. Add your bot token and your own Telegram user id to the "bot"
    section of config.ini.  It is required for free access to all bot
    commands.

    You also need to pass the bot token as a run parameter in test.sh.
    The bot.token value in config.ini will be deprecated soon, so it is
    not really required.

 5. Create a virtual environment.  For instance,

        python3 -m venv venv
        . venv/bin/activate

 6. Install all the dependencies with

        python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt

 7. Launch the bot with ./test.sh.

User guide
----------

Change the language with /lang LANGUAGE-ABBREVIATION.  Currently, only
English and Russian are supported.  For instance, "/lang ru" or
"/lang en".

User's role
-----------

Begin communication with the /start command.  You will be asked
for a username, so simply send /username YOUR-USERNAME.  It will be
seen by the cashier when you receive your order.

You can place a new order with /order DISHNAME QUANTITY.  Check
/menu for the available dishes before actually placing the order,
otherwise an error will be shown.

Cashier's role
--------------

You have to do the /start procedure and simply follow the user's
guide first.  Then, you need your administrator to assign you a
role.

After doing this, information about new orders will be sent to you.
Run /confirm ACCOUNT-NAME to close the order.  The account's name
can be found right in the order message.  Closing the order
decreases the number of available dishes in /menu.

Cook's role
-----------

You have to do the /start procedure and simply follow the user's
guide first.  Then, you need your administrator to assign you a
role.

You can add new dishes with /addish NAME PRICE QUANTITY (they will
show up in /menu, and consumers can find them there).

